  "body": "Found in the review read of PR #3668 (the catalog case `3d/rough-finish`, #2866). Read from the posted program and the model; no machine run. Refs #2392.\n\n**Case:** a 50 x 50 x 8 mm plate with a spherical dome (apex at Z18), box stock to Z22, 3D Pocket with a 6 mm flat end mill, stepdown 2 mm, stock to leave 0.5 mm.\n\n**What the program does:**\n- The level at Z18 is a full raster over the apex of the dome, which is at Z18. Line 83 (`G01 X24.48 Y-0.48 Z18.`) passes 0.0006 mm from the apex. The allowance there is 0, not 0.5 mm.\n- The last level is Z8, the top of the plate. The allowance on the floor is 0.\n- On the flanks the measured allowance is 0.21 mm to 0.38 mm (at Z16 the edge of the tool is 0.21 mm from the sphere), not 0.5 mm.\n\n**Expected:** the roughing leaves the stated allowance in each direction, or the operation has two values (wall and floor) and says which one it applies.\n\n**Risk:** the part is not cut below its surface. The finishing pass gets less material than the user stated, and on the floor and the apex it gets none.\n\n**Done when:** a test measures the smallest distance from the roughing path (tool envelope) to the model on this case, and it is not below the stated allowance less the tolerance. The catalog program `examples/catalog/3d/rough-finish/rough-finish.nc` is then made again.\n",
